{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgrn8886FECXJJdcnLdjG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015Ze8gwZ1M25mLTrT484XR9","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\Users\user\AppData\Local\Temp\claude-eval-GufJUW\home\cwd\docs\adr\0001-event-source-order-storage.md","content":"# Event-source order storage

Orders move from CRUD tables to an append-only event log, and all order read models are projected from it. Auditors must be able to replay any order's full history, and only event sourcing makes that history the source of truth instead of a side record that can drift from it.

## Considered Options

- **Audit table next to the CRUD tables**: rejected. The history is secondary to the current-state rows and can disagree with them, so it can't be relied on for replay.
- **Change data capture on the CRUD tables**: rejected. It records row changes, not business intent, and depends on capture infrastructure to keep the history complete.

## Consequences

Hard to reverse: going back to CRUD would mean rebuilding every read model.
