**Chosen name: Return.** It's now in `GLOSSARY.md`. "Cancellation" already means withdrawing a whole Order before Dispatch, so using "cancel" for a single item after it arrives would give one word two meanings. A **Return** is when one delivered Line Item is sent back and refunded on its own. I listed "cancel an item" and "partial cancellation" as terms to avoid, and added a short Relationships section that sets the two terms side by side.

**About "the rest of the plan":** the folder only contains `GLOSSARY.md`, with no plan, spec or code, so there's nothing further to carry on with. If the plan is somewhere else, point me to it.

These questions will decide what else the glossary needs:

